= Liquidity pool — Simple =

A liquidity pool is a shared reserve of assets used for trading or another financial function. In an AMM, traders swap against the pool. The pool is the assets; the AMM is the mechanism that prices and executes trades.

'''Important boundary:''' liquidity pool ≠ AMM.

